1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,000
One city has fired porcelain for 1,700 years.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,400
They call Jingdezhen China's porcelain capital.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,800
The old saying: white as jade, thin as paper.

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,200
Tap the rim — it rings like a chime.

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,600
By the classic count, 72 hands shape one piece.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,000
Ming emperors built a kiln just for the court.

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,400
Double-tap if you'd cradle one of these.

9
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,400
★ Expert Tip: buy at a kiln workshop, skip the tourist stalls.

10
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,000
Seventeen centuries — one city, one craft.

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,400
Follow for China's crafts, one city at a time.
